## What is wrong (one paragraph)

`parseTestToken` in the auth service (`:19`) accepts an unsigned `test_token_<base64>` that names its own user and role.
Its environment guard is a DENYLIST: `if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {` (`:21`) refuses only when `NODE_ENV` is
exactly `production`. So with `NODE_ENV` unset, or set to anything else such as `staging`, and `ENABLE_TEST_TOKENS=true`
(`:25`), `authenticate()` attaches the self-asserted user. The gateway's `parseTestToken` already uses an ALLOWLIST and
refuses unless `NODE_ENV` is `development` or `test`. **This task:** make the auth service's guard the same allowlist, so an
unset or unexpected `NODE_ENV` refuses the test token. Nothing else changes: the `ENABLE_TEST_TOKENS` opt-in (`:25`) stays,
and `development` and `test` keep working.

